# LLM token economy

Every turn is billed for the whole accumulated context: a file pulled in on
turn 10 of 40 is paid for thirty times. Save tokens wherever quality allows;
never leave work unfinished or a claim unverified to save them.

## Context

- Name specific files and lines; do not read a whole file without need. The
  `read-gate` hook denies `Read` of a file over 350 lines without a range and
  returns its outline: take the range from the outline, or locate with
  `grep -n` first.
- Fold big logs and command output through `grep`/`findstr`/`Select-String`
  up front; only a summary enters context. Never read a raw chat transcript.
- A full overview of a big file or tree goes to the `explore` subagent; only
  its report enters context.
- Fewer turns: independent tool calls in one turn; do not reread a file after
  editing it; summarise long output instead of pasting it.
- A long session gets expensive on every turn: at a natural break suggest
  summarising (`/summarize`) or a new chat with a short handoff (state, next
  steps, decisions, files and lines).

## Models and subagents

- Model is chosen before the first message and not switched mid-chat: a switch
  rebuilds the prompt cache.
- Subagents only for two or more independent pieces. Give them explicit
  context: what was read, what was tried, which files and lines.
- Recon and lookups on a cheaper/faster model; decisions and reviews on the
  strongest one. Reviewer is never the author.

## Task levels

Declare the level in one line before work; in doubt take the lower one.
Ceremony must not cost more than the edit.

| Level | Scope | Process |
|---|---|---|
| S | one place, the edit is clear | edit, verify, commit; no spec, plan or subagents |
| M | one chain across 2–5 files | design in chat, solo, review at the end |
| L | two or more independent pieces | spec → plan → executors + separate reviewer |
